# `twoarity/as_int.hero` as it stood until 2026-11-10: `value` bound past
# `printf`'s `...` at an `i64`, refused since panel 243's R1 (defect 2421) as
# crossing by value, where nothing holds it to what `printf` reads. The
# refusal lands HERE, on this module's `value`, in its own words, and the
# namesake binding of `as_text.hero`, the same C name at another shape, is
# told on its own line in its own: found by the name alone, one was told on
# the other's line, a false message (2026-10-17).

extern "stdio.h"
    function printf(format: cstr lent, value: i64) -> i32  #~ ffi_parameter_type

function say(format: str, value: i64) -> i32
    return printf(format: format.cstr(), value: value)
